  "name": "SSL/TLS Certificate Expiry Monitor",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "cb95391a-ea98-4f94-8fda-164bd736a188",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1584,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 888,
        "content": "## SSL/TLS Certificate Expiry Monitor\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow polls a central certificate inventory covering domains, APIs, and internal services, computes how many days remain until each certificate expires, and classifies it into OK / Watch / Warning / Critical. Healthy certificates are ignored, Watch/Warning certificates are packaged as a standard renewal reminder, and Critical certificates wait through a short dedup window before being packaged as an urgent renewal task and alert.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure certInventoryApiUrl and credentials in \"Fetch Certificate Inventory\" so it points at your cert-manager / CMDB / inventory service.\n- Set watchDaysThreshold, warningDaysThreshold, and criticalDaysThreshold in the config node to match your renewal SLAs.\n- Verify the inventory response shape matches what downstream nodes expect: { certificates: [ { domain, serviceType, owner, issuer, expiryDate, environment }, ... ] }.\n- Connect the two output Set nodes (\"Prepare Standard Renewal Reminder\" and \"Prepare Critical Renewal Task & Alert\") to your own notification/ticketing system (e.g. Jira, email, Slack) — they are left generic on purpose.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the day thresholds, the dedup wait duration on the critical path, and the renewal task fields to match your organization's certificate rotation process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a2cf3b61-4bd1-4907-9897-32978bc02b44",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1024,
        -432
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 512,
        "content": "## Start and configure scan\n\nProvides scheduled and manual entry points, then initializes shared workflow settings such as the inventory API and all expiry-day thresholds."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8be5923f-9232-4532-8396-4f9e8f56e6e9",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -576,
        -352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 624,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Fetch certificate inventory\n\nCalls the certificate inventory API for all monitored domains, APIs, and internal services, then waits briefly to let the response settle before processing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3463ec65-a676-42d8-bc10-8c1f32308578",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        80,
        -560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 464,
        "height": 528,
        "content": "## Split and classify\n\nSplits the inventory list into one item per certificate, then computes days-until-expiry and an urgency tier for each using the configured thresholds."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "35403658-f0ee-4edb-b000-b41a7d4fe099",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        592,
        -704
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 688,
        "height": 800,
        "content": "## Route by urgency\n\nHealthy certificates are dropped. Watch/Warning certificates are packaged as a standard renewal reminder. Critical certificates continue to the escalation path."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6acf0323-b2c9-4fa1-bfd3-8a91854c23bb",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1360,
        -336
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 624,
        "height": 512,
        "content": "## Critical escalation\n\nCritical certificates wait through a short dedup window (avoids re-alerting on every poll) before being packaged as an urgent renewal task."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f45b2fdd-077a-4b02-a227-385537962cb2",
